# `yo fix <path> --migrate unsized` with v0.2.78 over code written for
# v0.2.77, where a bare `Dyn(...)` was the owning box (decision 49 S2; the
# verdict of issues/fixed/2026-11-15-what-does-migrate-unsized-do-under-the-binary-that-flips-dyn.md).
# The syntactic pass still writes every one-line bare `Dyn(...)` type spelling
# as `Box(Dyn(...))` and lists a spelling over several lines (multi.yo). The
# evaluation cannot read the old file: a by-value `Dyn` is E0619 under
# v0.2.78, so no `dyn(v)` site is rewritten and both files are reported as not
# evaluating (rc 1). The upgrade path is v0.2.77's mode, which E0619's help
# names: `yo version install 0.2.77 && yo fix <path> --migrate unsized`.
fix . --migrate unsized
